### Image tag strategy per relevant service
| Container               | Image                                         | Tag kind         | Auto-update safe? |
|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|------------------|-------------------|
| nextcloud-app           | `nextcloud:31-fpm`                            | major-major.minor pinned (31.x patch) | yes within major |
| nextcloud-cron          | `nextcloud:31-fpm`                            | same as app      | yes within major  |
| nextcloud-web           | `nginx:alpine`                                | rolling          | yes               |
| nextcloud-db            | `postgres:16-alpine`                          | major pinned     | yes within major 16, NEVER bump to 17 |
| nextcloud-redis         | `redis:7-alpine`                              | major pinned     | yes within major 7 |
| immich_server           | `ghcr.io/immich-app/immich-server:release`   | tracks release   | yes (whitelist)   |
| immich_machine_learning | `ghcr.io/immich-app/immich-machine-learning:release` | tracks release | yes (whitelist) |
| immich_redis            | `docker.io/valkey/valkey:8-bookworm`          | major pinned     | yes within major 8 |
| immich_postgres         | `ghcr.io/tensorchord/pgvecto-rs:pg14-v0.2.0`  | **HARD-PINNED**  | **NEVER auto** — coupled to Immich release; pgvecto upgrades are migrations |
| jellyfin                | `jellyfin/jellyfin:latest`                     | fully unpinned   | yes               |

### Existing Watchtower (@ `compose/proxy.yml`)
- Container `compose-watchtower-1`, image `containrrr/watchtower`.
- Args: `--interval 3600 --label-enable --cleanup` (verified via `docker inspect`).
- `--label-enable` = OPT-IN per-container label `com.centurylinklabs.watchtower.enable=true`.
- `--cleanup` = **removes the OLD image after update** (so local rollback cache is gone).
- Currently ONLY `cliproxyapi` (proxy.yml) is enrolled. None of nextcloud/jellyfin/immich.
- Author notes the user investigated the watchtower-label mechanism in bash history.

### Existing backup: Kopia (also on iskradocker, separate from this project's CEA stack)
- Container `kopia`, image `kopia/kopia:latest`, up 3 weeks.
- Hourly snapshots with retention `latest,hourly,daily,weekly,monthly,annual` for:
  - `/backup/compose` (~48 KB — the compose dir) ✓
  - `/backup/nextcloud` (17.4 GB — nextcloud data) ✓
  - `/backup/photos` (78.8 GB — immich upload dir) ✓
  - `/backup/config` (1.1 GB — /srv/config) ✓
  - `/backup/docker.env` ✓
- Home dir backup script: `/home/antoine/docker/kopia-homelab-snapshot.sh` (homelab paths).
- B2 offsite: `/home/antoine/docker/kopia-sync-to-b2.sh`.

### NOT tracked by git
- `/home/antoine/docker` is NOT a git repo (verified: `git rev-parse` → fatal).

### Conventions documented in `compose/AGENTS.md`
- Compose location: `~/docker/compose/`
- Config persistence: `/srv/config/<service>/`
- Media storage: `/srv/storage1/`, `/srv/storage2/`
- LinuxServer.io images preferred, PUID=1000 PGID=1000.
- Restart policy: `unless-stopped` for all.
- Override env file via `~/docker/.env`.

## Topology lock (5 independent components)

| ID | Component | One-line outcome |
|----|-----------|------------------|
| C1 | Update mechanism choice | Pick automated cadence + provider (watchtower-extend / scheduled-script / manual). |
| C2 | Auto-update whitelist (which containers) | Decide which of the 10 target containers get auto vs manual handling. |
| C3 | Pre-update + rollback safety | Snapshot + image re-tag mechanism so a bad update is reversible in <5 min. |
| C4 | DB / pgvecto-rs special handling | Never auto-bump immich_postgres; document the per-Immich-release manual bump runbook. |
| C5 | Config version control | `/home/antoine/docker/compose/` becomes a git repo with `.gitignore` for `.env*`. |

## Forks surviving the two filters (owner-decisions)

### ASK (3 — owner-decisions, ranked by foggiest-gap)

**Fork 1 — Update mechanism (THE big fork).**
WHY: determines the entire approach; trades off convenience vs reversibility.
Default: scheduled cron script (weekly Sun 04:00 ET) that pulls+recreates+health-checks,
pre-snapshots via existing Kopia, pre-tags old image for rollback. Alternative: extend
existing Watchtower (zero-touch, but `--cleanup` removes old image → no rollback).

**Fork 2 — Notification model.**
WHY:илка화 user has 3 services with different down-impact; silent auto-apply vs
review-then-approve matters. Default: silent apply + email/Telegram on success/failure.
Alternative: notify-only (no auto-apply, user clicks apply) / full manual.

**Fork 3 — Maintenance-window awareness.**
WHY: 30s-2min downtime per service during recreate. Default: bind to Sun 04:00 ET.
Alternative: per-service windows / no window (immediate).

### ADOPTED AS DEFAULTS (announced, not asked)

- **Fork A (pgvecto/DB treatment):** HARD RULE — `immich_postgres` stays pinned at
  `pg14-v0.2.0`; `nextcloud-db` stays on `postgres:16-alpine`; both are EXCLUDED from
  any auto-update mechanism. Bumps per Immich's published minimum pgvecto version / per
  Postgres major-release migration runbook. Rationale: fact-based (Immich docs + Postgres
  major-upgrade docs), not a preference fork.
- **Fork B (rollback mechanism):** pre-update local image re-tag
  (`docker tag <name>:<tag> <name>:rollback-<ts>`) before each pull, kept for N=4 weeks.
  Plus existing Kopia hourly snapshots already cover data. The cron/job script does both.
- **Fork C (git init):** init `/home/antoine/docker/compose/` as git repo on iskradocker
  (`git init`, `.gitignore` `.env* *.backup *.bak*`); first commit captures current state.
  Complements (does not replace) Kopia `/backup/compose` hourly snapshots.
- **Fork D (test strategy):** each scheduled update job runs
  `docker compose -f <file>.yml up -d`, then health-check (`/health` or container health
  status), and auto-rollbacks on failure using the pre-tagged rollback image.

